    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0826" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.00/7–1444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-14T20:00:00-05:00">July 14, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1253. In connection with last paragraph of my telegram 1240 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">1254</hi>], July 13, 7 p.m.<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d773-f1"/> President López said to me today that what was needed
                    above everything here is a sufficient number of rifles for the national
                    police.</p>
                <pb facs="0827" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>
                <p>He confirmed to me what the Department and the Embassy have known for some time
                    that there is great friction between the army and the police. He said that the
                    recent developments have shown that the police is loyal to the Government and
                    that there is jealousy for that reason between the police and the army. He said
                    that his intention is if arms and ammunition can be obtained for the police to
                    declare publicly that Lend Lease material is being received for that
                    purpose.</p>
                <p>I consider the foregoing to be a most dangerous development in the internal
                    situation here. If news of this should reach the public and the army I am
                    apprehensive lest it might bring about a further and more serious revolt than
                    that which has just ended.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d773-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I respectfully suggest that this point of view be kept in mind in connection with
                    any requests which may be received for further arms and ammunition on behalf of
                    the police.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d773-f1" n="25" xml:id="d773-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d773-f2" n="27" xml:id="d773-f2-content">
                <p>The so-called Pasto Rebellion of July 10, 1944, which was suppressed and followed
                    by court martial proceedings against some 90 persons, of whom 65 were army
                    officers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
